# cuts/v1.0.38/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.38. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.38, by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh, and (since OS003 #114's treatment was
# extended to the cutter) by OS003 bin/cut.sh load_cut().
#
# THIS FILE IS THE AUTHORITATIVE HALF. OS003 carries a second cuts/v1.0.38/
# cut.env holding the operator's LOCAL PATHS (CM051_DIR, OSTLER_APP_PATH,
# CM044_DIR, HR015_DIR). They are deliberately different documents. Do not
# merge them: vendoring OS003's copy here was tried and reverted because it
# carried 464 lines of operator working record, four private box IPs and five
# notarisation submission IDs into this PUBLIC repo.
#
# WHY v1.0.38 EXISTS: THE COMPILER IS THE LAST OLD-NAMESPACE COMPONENT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The legacy-ontology-host -> schema.ostler.ai migration reaches a customer in
# THREE legs. The old hosts are named by DESCRIPTION and not spelled out here:
# scripts/verify_no_foreign_ontology_namespace.sh holds a HARD zero-occurrence
# ratchet on them, and only a file whose JOB is to police or perform that
# migration earns an exclusion from it. A cut record does neither, so it gets
# written this way. Do not helpfully restore the literals.
# Measured 2026-08-21 on origin/main fe6fe16, each with a positive control:
#
#   store   install.sh:19543-19546 runs migrate_graph_namespace.py --apply
#           unconditionally, every install, BEFORE the first writer.      IN
#   writer  vendor/ostler_fda: schema.ostler.ai 26, legacy ontology host 0,
#           legacy enrichment host 0 (control: 'def ' 318).               IN
#   reader  the pinned wiki-compiler, built from CM044 16bc4964:
#           legacy ontology host 22, schema.ostler.ai 0
#           (control: 'def ' 3465).                                      OUT
#
# So this tree would migrate the customer's store and then hand it a compiler
# querying the namespace it had just migrated AWAY from. Every pwg-sourced
# section renders EMPTY and nothing goes red. The wiki re-pin is the headline
# of this cut and it REPAIRS that, it does not risk it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DAEMON CHANGED. 0.4.58 -> 0.4.60, AND THE PIN IS DERIVED, NOT COPIED
#
# This section previously read "THE DAEMON IS UNCHANGED ... this cut rebuilds
# no daemon". That stopped being true on 2026-08-21 and the sentence is
# replaced rather than amended, because a stale reassurance is worse than a
# stale number: it tells the reader not to look.
#
# WHY IT CHANGED. The hub-v0.4.60 daemon CI built was Signature=adhoc,
# TeamIdentifier=not set, spctl-rejected and unstapled. It was rebuilt with
# ostler-assistant release/build-local.sh (which signs, notarises and staples)
# and promoted to ostler-ai/ostler-releases. The unsigned CI artefact is kept
# deliberately in ostler-assistant hub-v0.4.60 as the red fixture for the
# HR015 #837 signature gate; its release notes say so in terms. NEVER promote
# the ostler-assistant daemon tarball.
#
# Read out of the trees and the artefacts, cross-checked FOUR ways, because a
# version/checksum pair came apart on v1.0.29 with no gate watching it:
#
#     git rev-parse hub-v0.4.60^{}             8ba3e948edf957e3626158e8ed50edfdabefdd54
#     Ostler.app OSTLER_HUB_BUILD_COMMIT       8ba3e948edf957e3626158e8ed50edfdabefdd54
#     Ostler.app WRAPPER_FRONTEND_COMMIT       8ba3e948edf957e3626158e8ed50edfdabefdd54
#     daemon     DAEMON_FRONTEND_COMMIT        8ba3e948edf957e3626158e8ed50edfdabefdd54
#     gui/Makefile  DAEMON_VERSION             0.4.60
#     install.sh    OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION   0.4.60
#     install.sh    DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256 d6e94c89...8f4bba
#
# The last two of the four sentinels are the pair verify_commit_parity.sh
# actually compares, and they are read from the COMPILED binaries with the
# gate's own method, not from a build log. The Hub app had to be rebuilt at
# 8ba3e948 for exactly this reason: its frontend BYTES were already identical
# (both sides carry index-BJGHlmN_.js + index-C3vVbOBz.css), but the gate
# compares stamped commits, and the 0.4.58 wrapper was stamped 5b7efb00. A
# byte-identical frontend built from a different commit still reads as drift,
# correctly, because nothing in the artefact can tell the gate otherwise.
#
# hub-v0.4.60 is an ANNOTATED tag. The tag OBJECT is e9550dbe; recording that
# would pin to a tag rather than to source, so the value below is the
# DEREFERENCED commit.
#
# HUB_APP_SHA256 moved too (gui/Makefile). It is keyed off DAEMON_VERSION, so
# bumping the daemon renames the Hub app tarball as well. That asset did not
# exist at 0.4.60 when the re-pin was first attempted and the cut would have
# failed at download-hub-app.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon. hub-v0.4.60, signed, notarised and stapled. CHANGED in this cut.
DAEMON_COMMIT=8ba3e948edf9

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THE CM051 PIN BELOW IS PROVISIONAL AND WILL BE WRONG BY THE TAG.
#
# It names origin/main as it stood when this record was opened, BEFORE the wiki
# re-pin. That re-pin CHANGES install.sh, so this pin must be re-pointed after
# the last merge. v1.0.31 was burnt by a pin chosen early and trusted, and
# v1.0.37's preflight caught the same shape again -- its refusal text is worth
# keeping: "the pin IS an ancestor of the ref. That is not a defence. Ancestry
# proves ordering and says nothing about content."
#
# RE-VERIFY IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE TAG, AFTER THE LAST MERGE:
#     git rev-parse $CM051:install.sh
#     git rev-parse origin/main:install.sh
# Both must name the same blob. At the moment this file was written:
#     origin/main            fe6fe167040e27079b1fff5b7424b03d2e92e9b6
#     origin/main:install.sh dab40b2175be3e303ff6f45d91ab408ac53371b5
CM051=38670eb38bcce396194fa9705d8f24034a298c25
